// expect: 9
// A DECLARED anonymous rest. The residual `pick` carries on its own decl is
// a guess — an empty remainder from no closed partner — and the projection
// still says so; that half of this fixture stands and the mark is why the
// difference is legible at the query and the floor.
//
// What changed is which row the EMIT reads. This fixture was banked at 7 —
// `alpha`, the wrong slot — with its own instruction: "the fixture holds the
// CURRENT answer so the day it changes is a day someone chose". Today is
// that day and the choice was `Hβ.lower.open-row-field-offset-from-known-set`.
// The call proves the whole set at the site; the specialization walk keys the
// row var on it now, so the twin's receiver is closed and `u.zeta` reads
// zeta. 9, not 7 — the neighbouring value it used to return.
fn pick(u: {zeta: Int, ...}) = u.zeta
fn main(q) = pick({alpha: 7, zeta: 9})
